Backport of SQLite check-in 9e2caaa382 (trunk), "Fix the OPFS SAHPool VFS's
xLock/xUnlock to properly deal with multiple handles to the same underlying
file within a single thread", GitHub mirror commit
3b28aa1ce78a822befc17e90319d9231d403514c. Hunks are upstream's
ext/wasm/api/sqlite3-vfs-opfs-sahpool.c-pp.js diff verbatim, retargeted at the
built bundle: a per-path lock table (#mapPathToLock, modelled on
os_unix.c:unixInodeInfo) so a conflicting xLock returns SQLITE_BUSY, xClose
drops the handle's lock, hasReservedLock reads the table, and
releaseAccessHandles clears both maps. Without it two handles on one file in
the same thread could both write.
Drop this patch once the pinned SQLite release contains 9e2caaa382.

